WEBVTT

00:00:01.550 --> 00:00:03.220
<i>We've confirmed that the students are safe.</i>

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:05.610
<i>Seven wounded, none seriously.</i>

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:09.830
<i>One student and one teacher 
are unaccounted for.</i>

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:13.080
<i>According to one of the other students, 
they were flown out by helicopter.</i>

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.600
<i>Civil Aviation detected 
an unidentified helicopter,</i>

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:17.030
<i>but lost it near the border.</i>

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:23.320
What's the meaning of this? 
You want me to save Padar?

00:00:23.320 --> 00:00:27.640
As you know, Padar is split between the 
reform movement, spearheaded by the king,

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:30.260
and the traditionalists 
led by Padar's High Priest.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.470
I side with the reformers.

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:35.690
My father is correct when he says 
Padar must move with the times.

00:00:35.690 --> 00:00:40.250
My employers would rather avoid any 
reforms that could lead to internal strife.

00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:41.520
I see your game.

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:45.140
You were hoping to take me out in the chaos
caused by those terrorists, correct?

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:53.670
First, answer me this...

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:56.280
Why did you help me?

00:00:57.840 --> 00:00:59.980
Look. Amy's among them.

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.780
Isn't that Fujiko behind her?

00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:06.940
Let's move.

00:01:06.940 --> 00:01:08.210
Giving up?

00:01:08.210 --> 00:01:09.750
Don't be stupid.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:11.790
Then, where are we going?

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:15.210
Do I hafta spell it out 
for ya? I'm a thief.

00:01:15.950 --> 00:01:19.280
And I haven't bagged my score yet.

00:02:42.970 --> 00:02:47.020
<b>How To Steal A Kingdom</b>

00:02:47.010 --> 00:02:50.020
"Two weeks after the incident 
at the school in Annecy,"

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:53.100
"Princess Dolma has been
 successfully rescued"

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:57.660
"from her captors by the CIA 
and American special forces."

00:02:57.660 --> 00:02:59.020
That's their cover story, anyway.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:03.120
The CIA had a hand in 
the attack in the first place.

00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:07.650
The Whales of Liberation 
carried out the attack.

00:03:07.650 --> 00:03:11.650
But there's a good chance the CIA 
were looking to capitalize on it.

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:16.490
Are you saying the helicopter that 
airlifted Princess Dolma out was CIA?

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:21.040
Well, Padar is America's strategic 
bridgehead in South Asia.

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:25.050
Something must be going on in the country.

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:28.040
These clowns think they can 
just swoop in and swipe my loot?

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.520
I'll show them...

00:03:32.870 --> 00:03:35.930
Outside traffic isn't allowed 
in the new district.

00:03:36.570 --> 00:03:39.040
On one side of the river is the new district,

00:03:39.040 --> 00:03:42.190
constructed with the help of Shake Hands,
the world-famous IT company.

00:03:42.190 --> 00:03:45.940
On the other side, 
you have the old town.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:52.400
<i>What is your destination?</i>

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:53.640
Who goes there?!

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:56.600
Was it the car talking just now?

00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.870
<i>Mr. Daisuke Jigen. 
Welcome to the Kingdom of Padar.</i>

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:00.420
The hell?!

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:04.030
<i>Do you wish to go to the New Padar Hotel?</i>

00:04:04.030 --> 00:04:05.940
It knows our reservation, too?

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:07.930
What in the world is going on here?

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:11.710
Remember them asking us 
where we were staying at the border?

00:04:11.710 --> 00:04:17.430
The idea is to use our biometrics 
to service our every need in the city.

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:22.150
Wow, 100% self-driving, huh?

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.450
I guess we're in sci-fi country now.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:28.950
<i>This is a no-smoking area.</i>

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:35.950
<i>Please refrain from smoking or 
relocate to an authorized smoking area.</i>

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:40.340
Did I say sci-fi? More like a nanny state.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:45.960
Here.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:06.600
This is a lovely place, Ling.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:13.250
Seems you boys are another step 
closer to realizing your dream.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:14.870
Thank you, Fujiko.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:19.010
But where do we stand on
 that other dream of mine?

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:20.040
What other dream?

00:05:22.580 --> 00:05:25.060
Going to see the Northern Lights with you.

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:30.120
I didn't take you for the romantic type.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:33.150
What with the whole global IT 
business thing you've got going.

00:05:33.150 --> 00:05:35.350
I'm just a business partner.

00:05:35.350 --> 00:05:37.070
Enzo's the real hero.

00:05:37.070 --> 00:05:38.670
Can you get to the point?

00:05:38.670 --> 00:05:40.810
Adults waste too much time on small-talk.

00:05:42.310 --> 00:05:45.520
And children are too direct. 
Not to mention, rude.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:48.820
You want to know about
 Princess Dolma, right?

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.340
She's currently in the hospital.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.270
Was she injured?!

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:54.480
Psychologically, yes.

00:05:55.170 --> 00:06:00.100
She has acute stress disorder, brought on by 
getting caught up in that terrorist attack.

00:06:00.100 --> 00:06:03.180
She didn't seem that fragile.

00:06:03.180 --> 00:06:04.600
The picture is a bit murky.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:09.010
She's not allowed visitors. Even the 
king's been barred from seeing her.

00:06:10.820 --> 00:06:13.220
The king and his people haven't caught on yet.

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.230
We'll finally be able to take back Padar!

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.660
The princess's hospital 
is here in the old town.

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:28.680
So she can relax, supposedly.

00:06:28.680 --> 00:06:30.150
Piping hot!

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:32.480
Fresh fried samosas, get 'em here!

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:34.730
Oh, looks tasty!

00:06:34.730 --> 00:06:36.230
Can I get three?

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:36.960
Sure thing!

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.750
They're hot, so be careful.

00:06:39.100 --> 00:06:42.520
You're a photographer, ain't ya, mister? 
Here to snap pics of Princess Dolma?

00:06:42.520 --> 00:06:43.990
Is it that obvious?

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:46.430
Well, you don't look like a tourist.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:49.560
And foreigners on business 
stick to the new district.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.000
Quit being such a baby.

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:53.410
Hot, hot, hot!

00:06:54.110 --> 00:06:55.600
Yowch, that's hot!

00:06:56.700 --> 00:06:59.280
The samosas are on the house...

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:02.040
Just, please... don't go trackin' 
down Princess Dolma.

00:07:02.040 --> 00:07:05.040
People around here really care 
about the princess, huh?

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:08.670
Before she was shipped off to boarding 
school, she used to come by a lot.

00:07:10.020 --> 00:07:14.620
She looked so happy, eating her samosas.

00:07:14.620 --> 00:07:16.580
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

00:07:16.580 --> 00:07:17.290
Pass.

00:07:18.800 --> 00:07:20.120
Hot! Hot!

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:27.620
I heard this from a trustworthy source...

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:28.100
No security cameras in this day and age...

00:07:28.100 --> 00:07:30.120
What an analog hospital.

00:07:31.890 --> 00:07:32.730
See you around!

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:35.770
She's not in the hospital.

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:37.230
Used your feminine wiles again?

00:07:37.710 --> 00:07:43.060
People with smarts become scholars, 
people with fast legs become athletes...

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.090
What's wrong with playing to your strengths?

00:07:45.090 --> 00:07:47.230
What can I get you ladies?

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:48.480
I'll have a cup of chai.

00:07:48.880 --> 00:07:49.980
I want...

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:53.480
...buttered Padar yak stew.

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:56.910
What's that?

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:57.490
Dol—

00:08:00.610 --> 00:08:03.310
A friend of mine made it for me once.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.130
She said it was a Padar specialty.

00:08:06.130 --> 00:08:08.190
I'm impressed you've heard of it!

00:08:08.190 --> 00:08:11.750
But we don't serve it here. Most places don't.

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:12.500
Why not?

00:08:12.770 --> 00:08:15.490
Padar yaks are servants of the gods.

00:08:15.870 --> 00:08:21.240
It's a very special dish you should only 
eat with your nearest and dearest.

00:08:22.440 --> 00:08:23.520
<i>Dolma...</i>

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.340
A princess, miraculously rescued...

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:40.550
...from the clutches of the terrorists
 who had kidnapped her...

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.890
And a cute one, at that.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:48.590
Any picture of her would be 
front-page fodder, for sure.

00:08:48.590 --> 00:08:51.850
Sounds like prime paparazzi bait.

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:54.730
And yet, no pictures have surfaced.

00:08:54.730 --> 00:08:57.050
They cannot photograph 
someone they cannot find.

00:08:57.050 --> 00:09:00.830
So where would the paparazzi 
have trouble getting into?

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:03.060
Places run by the military is my first guess.

00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:08.180
Reporting in from assignment!

00:09:18.150 --> 00:09:19.280
Many happy returns.

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:22.570
Today's your birthday, right?

00:09:22.570 --> 00:09:24.070
Y-Yeah... thanks.

00:09:26.840 --> 00:09:28.460
Looks like it was that guy's birthday.

00:09:28.460 --> 00:09:31.180
Boy, now I feel guilty for what we did.

00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:32.240
Wait a minute!

00:09:36.690 --> 00:09:40.810
Tomorrow, 1700 hours... 
There's going to be a special exercise.

00:09:40.810 --> 00:09:41.970
Be ready.

00:09:43.820 --> 00:09:44.990
What was that all about?

00:09:44.990 --> 00:09:47.090
Soldiers whispering among themselves...

00:09:47.570 --> 00:09:51.130
And there's a beef between the 
reformers and the traditionalists.

00:09:51.130 --> 00:09:52.120
Add it all together and...

00:09:52.120 --> 00:09:53.450
A coup d'état.

00:10:17.020 --> 00:10:18.700
High Priest, Your Excellency,

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.490
the CO of the 8th Artillery 
Regiment has joined our cause.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.270
We're using an emergency 
urban-training exercise...

00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.740
as a pretense for 
mobilizing our allied forces.

00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:30.000
What about the Shake Hands corporation?

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:36.200
Don't worry, sir. We have avoided 
all internet communication.

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.070
Those capitalist misers won't 
have free reign over Padar.

00:10:48.600 --> 00:10:51.410
We've just received word from our superiors.

00:10:51.850 --> 00:10:54.740
America's going to maintain 
its neutral stance in public,

00:10:54.740 --> 00:10:58.280
but behind the scenes, 
it will be supporting the coup.

00:10:58.280 --> 00:11:01.920
Just what I'd expect from the CIA. 
Conspiracies are an old hat for you gentlemen.

00:11:01.920 --> 00:11:05.590
I want to apologize for the changes 
in the plan regarding Princess Dolma.

00:11:05.590 --> 00:11:08.720
I'm not about to deny 
a request from our sponsors.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:12.050
As long as I am the true 
authority, I have no issues.

00:11:12.050 --> 00:11:14.880
Of course, High Priest, Your Excellency.

00:11:18.670 --> 00:11:22.310
A freaking coup d'état? 
This has turned into a real drag.

00:11:22.720 --> 00:11:24.250
What now, Lupin?

00:11:24.250 --> 00:11:27.870
What's the problem? This just means 
we're dealing with fellow thieves.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:31.330
The only difference is <i>they</i> want 
the country, and <i>I</i> want the girl.

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.760
I'm not gonna let them show me up.

00:11:34.460 --> 00:11:37.650
And here I thought you 
were after a necklace...

00:11:49.590 --> 00:11:51.510
<i>This is the 5th Airborne Regiment.</i>

00:11:51.510 --> 00:11:53.760
<i>We're ready to descend on 
the designated control point.</i>

00:11:58.100 --> 00:12:00.420
This is the 2nd Combat 
Engineering Regiment.

00:12:00.420 --> 00:12:03.080
We're ready to blow the fiber-optic cables.

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:07.850
Try to hurry.

00:12:07.850 --> 00:12:08.490
Right.

00:12:10.520 --> 00:12:12.640
The hive is buzzing, it seems.

00:12:12.640 --> 00:12:16.310
I hear sight and hearing are the 
first things to go when you get old.

00:12:16.960 --> 00:12:19.500
Girl, do you have a problem with me?

00:12:19.990 --> 00:12:20.990
I do.

00:12:20.990 --> 00:12:22.350
Why?

00:12:35.160 --> 00:12:37.180
The coup d'état is under way.

00:12:37.590 --> 00:12:41.020
In six hours' time, you will be queen.

00:12:41.020 --> 00:12:42.440
And a puppet.

00:13:10.650 --> 00:13:13.830
<i>The Ministry of Home Affairs and the 
Central Police HQ are both under our control.</i>

00:13:14.300 --> 00:13:16.810
<i>The ministers for finance 
and trade are in custody, too.</i>

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:19.260
<i>Commencing occupation of the 
Royal Communication Center.</i>

00:13:19.260 --> 00:13:22.870
<i>The royal guards are staying neutral. 
No sign of any movement from them.</i>

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:28.000
A request for an audience with 
His Excellency, the High Priest.

00:13:28.000 --> 00:13:29.390
At a time like this?

00:13:29.390 --> 00:13:30.610
Get rid of him!

00:13:31.660 --> 00:13:35.070
I'm here because I heard Lupin 
sent one of his calling cards.

00:13:35.740 --> 00:13:36.820
Who's this?!

00:13:37.230 --> 00:13:38.990
You can't just barge in here!

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:40.630
And who might you be?

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.780
I'm Zenigata with the ICPO.

00:13:43.150 --> 00:13:46.290
Lupin's after the Bloody Teardrop.

00:13:46.290 --> 00:13:48.840
Oh, I thought that was 
some kind of prank...

00:13:49.710 --> 00:13:53.040
But the Bloody Teardrop isn't here.

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:55.540
Princess Dolma has it.

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:58.840
You're suggesting Lupin sent 
a calling card to the wrong location?

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:01.390
It seems that way.

00:14:05.620 --> 00:14:09.960
I know Lupin, and while he may 
be a fool, he's not stupid.

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:13.150
If he says it's here, it <i>must </i>be here!

00:14:10.920 --> 00:14:12.440
Hey, stop right there!

00:14:13.150 --> 00:14:14.870
Are you calling His Excellency a liar?!

00:14:17.770 --> 00:14:22.980
Well, if you insist, 
you can join our security detail.

00:14:22.980 --> 00:14:25.620
After all, you seem well-acquainted 
with this Lupin character.

00:14:25.980 --> 00:14:27.410
It'd be my pleasure.

00:14:27.410 --> 00:14:28.740
Amur...

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:29.510
Sir!

00:14:29.510 --> 00:14:34.140
Give the inspector an overview 
of the palace's security.

00:14:34.500 --> 00:14:35.640
At once, sir!

00:14:42.490 --> 00:14:44.740
No security cameras at all?

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:48.440
Our palace has used only traditional 
methods for six-hundred years.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:51.880
Besides, using machines makes 
you dependent on them.

00:14:51.880 --> 00:14:53.600
There's wisdom in that.

00:14:53.600 --> 00:14:55.980
Not much for a hacker 
to sink their teeth into.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:15:00.920
And six-hundred years... 
That's a lot of tradition.

00:15:02.520 --> 00:15:04.470
And this palace is a 
love letter to tradition!

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:07.210
You idiot!

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:11.770
Hey, thanks for the tour.

00:15:11.770 --> 00:15:12.680
Son of a...

00:15:12.680 --> 00:15:15.150
Wanna tell me where Princess Dolma is?

00:15:15.150 --> 00:15:15.860
Search me.

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:20.260
Okay, how about anywhere that's 
been declared off-limits lately?

00:15:20.620 --> 00:15:24.740
You really wanna die here? 
Wouldn't that make your family sad?

00:15:25.230 --> 00:15:29.480
You all looked really happy in 
that picture in your wallet...

00:15:30.010 --> 00:15:31.180
Right, "Papa"?

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:37.140
The west tower.

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:38.120
Thanks ever so much!

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:42.490
Now, then...

00:15:48.970 --> 00:15:53.010
Time to wrap this up before they catch on.

00:15:53.550 --> 00:15:56.850
Zenigata with the ICPO. That's right.

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.010
Get me everything you can.

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:01.020
What's wrong?

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:02.980
I think it's caught on something.

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:05.840
The right wheel's stuck.

00:16:05.840 --> 00:16:07.010
Man...

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.280
<i>Wait for me, Dolma!</i>

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:22.100
And the backup line?

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:24.110
It's good. We checked it the other day.

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:32.840
Shut down all access to 
the internet immediately.

00:16:32.840 --> 00:16:36.010
If you truly love your country, 
you <i>will </i>cooperate.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:41.010
I'm heading to the west tower.

00:16:42.300 --> 00:16:46.770
It's about time our heroine 
entered the picture.

00:16:57.640 --> 00:16:58.400
<i>I looked down!</i>

00:17:06.120 --> 00:17:09.410
<i>Pull it together... 
Fujiko would laugh at you.</i>

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:29.490
Isn't it a bit late for you to be out?

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:33.730
Schoolgirls should be at home at this hour.

00:17:35.110 --> 00:17:38.540
You don't get to pretend you're a 
teacher anymore. Where's Dolma?

00:17:38.540 --> 00:17:40.740
You think you have a fighting chance here?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:42.500
You're being filmed right now.

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:46.460
Do you want footage of a CIA agent 
shooting a civilian to appear online?

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:52.330
I'm afraid that bluff 
doesn't make the grade.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.230
It won't be earning you any credits.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:02.440
You couldn't have made it in here alone.

00:18:03.340 --> 00:18:06.080
Tell me who you're working with.

00:18:10.410 --> 00:18:11.920
<i>Save me...</i>

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:12.860
<i>Anyone...</i>

00:18:12.860 --> 00:18:14.720
Any... one...

00:18:14.720 --> 00:18:15.950
Lupin!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.850
How immature... Give it a rest.

00:18:25.860 --> 00:18:27.170
You...

00:18:27.170 --> 00:18:28.500
Lupin III.

00:18:29.010 --> 00:18:33.510
Here to engage His Excellency, 
the High Priest, in a thieving competition.

00:18:36.760 --> 00:18:38.170
You okay, Amy?

00:18:38.570 --> 00:18:42.060
Good grief. It was crazy to try to do this solo.

00:18:42.060 --> 00:18:42.740
Lupin...

00:18:42.740 --> 00:18:44.940
Stop right there, Lupin.

00:18:44.940 --> 00:18:48.260
Keep on yapping, American lapdog. 
What are you even doing here?

00:18:48.260 --> 00:18:54.260
You CIA goons are pulling the strings 
behind this entire coup, aren't you?

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:58.420
Probably in the name of "world peace" 
or some other self-congratulatory crap...

00:18:58.420 --> 00:19:02.020
But all you ever really want is to make 
things more convenient for yourselves.

00:19:02.610 --> 00:19:05.450
Compared to guys like me, 
who freely admit to being crooks,

00:19:05.450 --> 00:19:07.040
you're several degrees nastier.

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.320
Shut up.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:08.840
Lupin—

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.030
Oh, you can't silence <i>me</i>.

00:19:10.430 --> 00:19:14.370
You think you're untouchable just because 
you're a sizable country, with the best army,

00:19:14.370 --> 00:19:16.540
and mountains of cash, is that it?

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:19.540
Get over yourselves!

00:19:19.540 --> 00:19:21.800
Whatever you're stalling for, it won't work.

00:19:21.800 --> 00:19:22.920
Ah, put a sock in it.

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.420
If you're gonna be a lapdog, 
then stick to howling like one.

00:19:39.400 --> 00:19:43.710
See? That's the thing about working 
for royalty. You gotta take it seriously.

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.250
Lupin!

00:19:45.250 --> 00:19:47.470
Hey, Amy. You okay?

00:19:47.470 --> 00:19:48.960
What are you doing here?

00:19:48.960 --> 00:19:50.210
I came for you.

00:19:54.360 --> 00:19:58.510
Stop with the dumb jokes. Saving Dolma is—

00:19:59.530 --> 00:20:00.610
Dolma!

00:20:04.710 --> 00:20:07.430
I came to save you. Let's get out of here.

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:08.590
Why are you here?

00:20:10.010 --> 00:20:11.320
Because we're friends.

00:20:15.890 --> 00:20:18.650
Hey, we're in the middle of 
a heart-warming reunion here.

00:20:19.480 --> 00:20:21.820
Could you maybe not ruin it?

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:29.740
What... the...

00:20:35.730 --> 00:20:37.260
But... why?

00:20:40.580 --> 00:20:44.170
Run... A-my...

00:20:48.220 --> 00:20:49.490
Lupin!

00:22:17.040 --> 00:22:18.560
Fujiko Mine here.

00:22:18.560 --> 00:22:20.810
Amy, Lupin's hurt.

00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:22.910
He can't come and save you anymore.

00:22:22.910 --> 00:22:25.080
Martial law has been declared in the city,

00:22:25.080 --> 00:22:28.410
and gunfire is raining down on
its formerly peaceful streets.

00:22:28.810 --> 00:22:33.950
Listen... In a warzone, 
a girl has to protect herself.

00:22:33.950 --> 00:22:37.160
That goes for young girls, 
as well as incomparable beauties.

00:22:37.990 --> 00:22:40.650
Next time: Her Relationship With Lupin.

00:22:38.000 --> 00:22:45.000
<b>Her Relationship With Lupin</b>

00:22:40.650 --> 00:22:44.230
If you can't manage that, then there's 
not much you can do to help him.
